MONZERO @RELEASE_TITLE@ - WINDOWS GRAPHICAL WALLET

Run start-wallet-gui.bat or monzero-wallet-gui.exe. This package includes the
matching @RELEASE_SHORT@ daemon and command-line tools and uses the Monzero genesis
network identity.

The graphical wallet starts its managed local daemon in synchronizing mode
and selects the local RPC endpoint automatically. New users do not need to
enter 127.0.0.1 or configure a remote node. Bootstrap RPC is only a temporary
fallback while the local blockchain catches up.

Wallet files: this release opens only wallet files created by Monzero.
Monero and other CryptoNote wallet files are refused. Wallets created by
earlier Genesis prereleases open normally, except those that had selected
the atomic-XMZ display unit; restore those from their recovery seed.
Amounts are always shown in XMZ with 11 decimal places.

This GUI is unsigned and unaudited prerelease software. It was cross-compiled
in the static Windows build environment defined by the GUI source's
Dockerfile.windows. Verify SHA256SUMS before running any executable.

The GUI source is the newest GUI commit whose Qt/wallet_api calls are all
satisfied by this core source tree. It deliberately excludes later, unmerged
GUI work (asset transfer/burn and DEX prototypes) that this core does not
implement.

GUI source:  @GUI_COMMIT@
Core source: @CORE_COMMIT@
